---
import { getPosts } from '../lib/site';
const latest = (await getPosts()).slice(0, 6);
---
<aside class="sidebar">
  <section>
    <img class="portrait" src="/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/mags-sikora-SEO-expert-london-300x300.webp" alt="Mags Sikora, SEO expert, London" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" />
    <h2>Hi, I'm Mags.</h2>
    <p>I dedicate this website to <a href="/">teach entrepreneurs</a> how to succeed online through SEO! Signup to my newsletter to get more tips how to grow your traffic faster.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Let's get connected!</h2>
    <p>Here I share both business and personal updates.</p>
    <ul class="social">
      <li><a href="https://twitter.com/magssikora" style="background:#83bac8" aria-label="Twitter" rel="noopener">Tw</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/c/Sheknowsdigital" style="background:#e34d2f" aria-label="YouTube" rel="noopener">YT</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/sheknowsdigital/?hl=en" style="background:#5a6678" aria-label="Instagram" rel="noopener">IG</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Free resources</h2>
    <a class="promo" href="/seo-checklist-blog-post-writing/">Write Google friendly blog posts: the SEO checklist</a>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Latest blog posts</h2>
    <ul class="latest">
      {latest.map((p) => <li><a href={`/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
</aside>
